    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21940020
    description: "Archived releases, all versions"
keywords:
  - Ingenuity Pathway Analysis
  - pathway analysis
  - bioinformatics
  - command-line tool

# No `version:`, `date-released:` or per-version DOI on purpose. All three are
# per-release facts that would need editing on every tag, and the per-version
# DOI proved the point: it named 1.0.0 and stayed that way through 1.0.1,
# 1.1.0, 1.2.0 and 1.3.0. Zenodo never imported it, so the archive was never
# wrong -- but GitHub's citation widget reads this file, and it showed a DOI
# labelled as the current version when it was three releases behind.
#
# The one DOI listed is the CONCEPT doi. Zenodo redirects it to whichever
# version is newest: minted with 1.0.0, it already resolves to 1.3.0. So a
# citation taken from here is never stale and this file never needs touching
# at release time. Zenodo takes the version from the git tag.
